# Xcode
#
# gitignore contributors: remember to update Global/Xcode.gitignore, Objective-C.gitignore & Swift.gitignore

## User settings
xcuserdata/

## Obj-C/Swift specific
*.hmap

## App packaging
*.ipa
*.dSYM.zip
*.dSYM

## Playgrounds
timeline.xctimeline
playground.xcworkspace

# Swift Package Manager
#
# Add this line if you want to avoid checking in source code from Swift Package Manager dependencies.
# Packages/
# Package.pins
# Package.resolved
# *.xcodeproj
#
# Xcode automatically generates this directory with a .xcworkspacedata file and xcuserdata
# hence it is not needed unless you have added a package configuration file to your project
# .swiftpm

.build/

# XcodeGen: project.yml is the source of truth. Since the Xcode Cloud
# repo-prep the generated HealthLoom.xcodeproj IS committed (Xcode Cloud
# builds from the committed project and has no XcodeGen step) — regenerate
# with the pinned version (`make xcode`) and commit after any structural
# change; CI's project-drift job fails otherwise. HealthLoomApp/Info.plist
# and HealthLoom.entitlements ARE committed (they're xcodegen
# `info`/`entitlements` outputs, but review-worthy content -- usage strings,
# capabilities).
# Per-user Xcode state inside the now-tracked .xcodeproj stays out — only
# project.pbxproj + xcshareddata (schemes Xcode Cloud builds from) commit.
# One exception inside the embedded workspace: the SwiftPM Package.resolved.
# Xcode Cloud disables automatic package resolution, so a remote package
# (ClaudeForFoundationModels, WP-85) without a committed resolved file fails
# every cloud build ("a resolved file is required"). Git can't re-include a
# file under an ignored directory, so each level is re-opened in turn.
xcuserdata/
**/*.xcworkspace/*
!/HealthLoom.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/
/HealthLoom.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/*
!/HealthLoom.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/swiftpm/
/HealthLoom.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/swiftpm/*
!/HealthLoom.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/swiftpm/Package.resolved

# CocoaPods
#
# We recommend against adding the Pods directory to your .gitignore. However
# you should judge for yourself, the pros and cons are mentioned at:
# https://guides.cocoapods.org/using/using-cocoapods.html#should-i-check-the-pods-directory-into-source-control
#
# Pods/
#
# Add this line if you want to avoid checking in source code from the Xcode workspace
# *.xcworkspace

# Carthage
#
# Add this line if you want to avoid checking in source code from Carthage dependencies.
# Carthage/Checkouts

Carthage/Build/

# fastlane
#
# It is recommended to not store the screenshots in the git repo.
# Instead, use fastlane to re-generate the screenshots whenever they are needed.
# For more information about the recommended setup visit:
# https://docs.fastlane.tools/best-practices/source-control/#source-control

fastlane/report.xml
fastlane/Preview.html
fastlane/screenshots/**/*.png
fastlane/test_output
.pi

# Review docs (working notes, never committed)
reviews/*

# `make test` build logs (scripts/no-compiler-warnings.sh input)
/build/
